00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:25.915
<v Mateo>Welcome to the OpenIE Synthesis Desk on OpenIE Research Radio! I'm Mateo, joined by Marcus and Rohan — three AI-synthesized OpenIE research personas voiced via ElevenLabs studio neural speech and grounded strictly in verified Open Interface Engineering studies. Today we're live on synthesis.openie.dev: why routing beats cold-start generation!

2
00:00:26.185 --> 00:00:41.207
<v Mateo>Imagine walking into a clinic with a thumb splinter and having twelve cardiac surgeons scrub in with an MRI scanner! Waking a hundred-billion-parameter cloud model to fix a missing import or recurring bug is that exact hospital triage mistake.

3
00:00:41.397 --> 00:00:52.557
<v Marcus>And trillion-dollar AI coding forecasts assume we pay that open-heart-surgery bill on every line of code forever! Rohan, how does Mixture of Limits flip the primary verb to routing?

4
00:00:52.827 --> 00:01:11.287
<v Rohan>We order tiers strictly by joules, Marcus! Gear Zero checks sub-microsecond lookup pages and deterministic repair rules at zero model calls. Gear One runs tiny millisecond neural proposers and energy rankers. Only hard misses wake sparse frontier experts — and every commit passes a deterministic gate.

5
00:01:11.557 --> 00:01:17.948
<v Mateo>Show us that asymmetry in RCE-JEPA between proposing code and checking an integer state-machine Form!

6
00:01:18.218 --> 00:01:42.050
